unlikely.",{"_":54,"ana":55,"ref":56},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":58,"dimensions":59},"Serifs used, deeply and neatly carved, although consistency of the width of carving varies slightly (esp. in the first letter). The two letters here are of different heights. No letter survives in its entirety.",[60,66],{"type":61,"l":62,"from":63,"to":63,"h":64,"unit":65},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","I at least 97mm, B at least 76mm","mm",{"type":67,"l":68,"from":63,"to":69,"unit":65},"interlinear","Interlineation line 1 to 2","line2",{"_":71,"notBefore":72,"notAfter":73},"Imperial -excellent letters\n                                (?)",1,300,[75,81],{"_":76,"type":77,"ref":78,"cert":79,"region":80},"Thermae Himeraeae","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462513","low","Sicilia",{"_":82,"type":83,"ref":84,"region":80},"Termini Imerese","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/6539140",[86],[87,88],37.98365,13.69555,{"_":90,"type":91,"subtype":92,"geo":20},"The place, date, and circumstances of the discovery are unknown, but the inscription is assumed to come from Termini Imerese","found","discovered",[],{"_":95,"type":96,"subtype":97,"when":98,"resp":99,"geo":20},"Antoniou, 2023-07-06. In the Depositi of Museo Civico Baldassare Romano, room 1, scaffold 13, shelf 3","observed","autopsied","2023-07-06","#AA",[101,108],{"n":102,"url":103,"height":104,"width":105,"desc":106,"surfaceType":107},"screen","ISic000256_tiled.tif","3680px","5520px","I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2023-07-06","front",{"n":102,"url":109,"height":104,"width":105,"desc":106,"surfaceType":110},"ISic000256_rear_tiled.tif","rear","Sicily",{"_":113,"role":114,"ref":115,"museum":116},"Museo Civico Baldassare Romano","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/066",{"slug":117,"type":114,"name":113,"uri":115,"description":118,"location":119},"066","A large and well-displayed collection. It begins with three ante-rooms, in the first of which is a rich display of lithics (mainly Neolithic) from the surrounding area. A display of material from Himera (lion-head spouts from the Temple of Victory and red-figure craters being the principle pieces) and a numismatic gallery then follow before the main room which contains Hellenistic and Roman material from Termini Imerese itself. Small finds, sculpture and inscriptions predominate. The museum collection continues upstairs with non-archaeological material (and a single inscription). The courtyard of the building holds a large collection of architectural pieces and inscriptions",{"settlement":82,"region":120,"country":121,"address":122,"geo":123},"Palermo","Italy","Via Marco Tullio Cicerone, 90018 - Termini Imerese (PA)",{"lat":124,"lon":125},37.98655109,13.69587845,{"_":127,"type":128},"16","inventory",{"_":130,"mainLang":131,"languages":132},"Latin","la",[130],{"type":134,"bibl":135},"edition",[136,20],{"type":137,"n":138,"author":139,"date":140,"citedRange":141,"ptr":142,"ref":144,"inscriptionDate":140,"year":38},"corpus","ILMusTermini","Bivona","1994","182",{"target":143},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/JCV85C79",{"_":145,"target":145},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002137",{"type":147,"bibl":148},"discussion",[20],{"editor":150,"principal":153,"contributors":154,"change":182},{"_":151,"ref":152},"Jonathan Prag","#JP",{"_":151,"ref":152},[155,158,162,166,170,174,178],{"_":151,"xml:id":156,"ref":157},"JP","http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":159,"xml:id":160,"ref":161},"James Cummings","JCu","http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6686-3728",{"_":163,"xml:id":164,"ref":165},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":167,"xml:id":168,"ref":169},"Valentina Mignosa","VM","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511",{"_":171,"xml:id":172,"ref":173},"Alex Antoniou","AA","http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7077-0703",{"_":175,"xml:id":176,"ref":177},"Alessia Coccato","Coccato","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6641-2820",{"_":179,"xml:id":180,"ref":181},"Robert Crellin","RC","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0100-7437",{"_":183,"when":184,"who":185},"Robert Crellin provided lemmatizations","2026-06-10","#RC",{"n":102,"url":103,"height":104,"width":105,"desc":106,"surfaceType":107},[],[189],"Bivona, 1994, ILMusTermini",[191],"JCV85C79",[193,194,195,22,27,31,196,197,198,199,197,200,201,131],"isic000256","i.sicily inscription 000256",{"_":5},"thermae himeraeae","termini imerese","sicilia","sicily","museo civico baldassare romano","latin",[],{"title":204,"body":205,"divs":206,"editions":231,"images":250,"handnote":261},"ISic000256. I.Sicily inscription 000256","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"la\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] BI \u003Cbr id=\"al-interpretive\">[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Robert Crellin\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive-simple-lemmatized\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\"> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span> ] BI [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cbr id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]BI\u003Cbr id=\"al-diplomatic\">[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Robert Crellin\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic-simple-lemmatized\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]BI[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003Ca href=\"ISic000256_tiled.tif\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2023-07-06\" src=\"ISic000256_tiled-thumb.tif\">\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"ISic000256.jpg\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2023-07-06\" src=\"ISic000256-thumb.jpg\">\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"ISic000256_rear_tiled.tif\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2023-07-06\" src=\"ISic000256_rear_tiled-thumb.tif\">\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"ISic000256_rear.jpg\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2023-07-06\" src=\"ISic000256_rear-thumb.jpg\">\u003C/a>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>Text of autopsy\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"1\">1: \u003Cspan>Bivona: si]BI?\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2> translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Given the size of the letters, the end of a name, such as Baebi, seems much more likely than a pronoun such as sibi or tibi (and, contra Bivona, there is no indication of an apex on the I, only the taller letter). The traces visible above the preserved line do not seem to be formal letters.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Bivona 1975-1976 556 no.27 tav.12 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Bivona 1994 182 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002137\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002137\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> \u003Cp>Serifs used, deeply and neatly carved, although consistency of the width of carving varies slightly (esp. in the first letter). The two letters here are of different heights. No letter survives in its entirety.\u003C/p> Line 1  I at least 97mm, B at least 76mm  Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[207,210,213,216,219,222,225,228],{"id":208,"html":209},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa, Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"la\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al-interpreti